==============================================================================
READING
==============================================================================
  Both runs are serial single-chain (one .1.txt each, no MPI), so the R-1 reported
  is a within-chain split statistic rather than the between-chain Gelman-Rubin the
  0.05 target is normally calibrated for. That makes the forecast optimistic, not
  pessimistic: a split-chain diagnostic understates the disagreement a second,
  independently seeded chain would expose.

  The fitted exponents are steeper than -0.5 because both runs are still in the
  transient where the proposal is being learned -- eleven 'Learn + convergence test'
  events so far. That rate is not sustainable; the asymptotic column is the one to
  plan against, and on it neither run reaches 0.05 before the cap.
